Neutral male gnomish Caveman
Gnome so that I can ascend a zen in each race as well as role.

Conducts 3 : wishless(2) and polyitemless.

It was a flawless zen since I never had my towel stolen/removed by
mistake. The wishless conduct was not intended at the start of game,
but as it was progressing I recognized and took the opportunity.
However I only decided to really go for it when I found my first bag,
in the Valley.

dumplog:
http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/g/graysocks/dumplog/1314025153.nh343.txt

Total number of games : 1348
Number of games with starting blindfold/towel : 10

This was not a particularly troublesome role/race. With a decent
constitution comes better HP. I would also get Mjollnir which proved
sufficient. One problem for caveman is starting with 0MC (specially
with werefoo), but I found a cloak of protection on DL1. Another bonus
was the number of general stores (the first on DL3) which eased
identification.

On Dl1, while running back and forth searching for a floating eye, a
death drop gave me my first magic marker.
After getting telepathy I headed for the mines. Minetown had a
cross-aligned altar; there was also a couple of elves who got me to 2
HP and gave me my first mithril (cursed -1). I had been killing random
dwarfs but no dwarvish mithril so far.

Back on the main dungeon, I found a co-aligned altar at DL6. After
exploring sokoban and getting the "oR, I did some price ID and BUC
test, and id'd B!ObjectDetection and a non cursed ring which was
either =PolC or =TelC. Back to the altar I got Mjollnir (and
trollsbane, while reseting prayer timeout).

Exploring the dungon I hit a poly trap, thus breaking polyselfless
(and cursed armor) and identifying =TC. Luckily my towel was of the
same material as Hulk's pants and it still fit my Yellow Dragon head.
I started eating tengus, so soon I got teleportitis, but never got
intrinsic teleport control.

When I explored the rest of the mines to get the luckstone I also
found a useless magic lamp which I fortunately decided to save for
later.

After a bit more of exploration and finding a mind flayer at DL 14, I
decided to return to the stash to do some ID. Luckily I had 2
?oGenocide (used for Mind-flayer and Master Mind-flayer) and a magic
marker at 0:67 (wrote 1 B?oG for L and one C?oG for Gray Dragon scale
mail). I also used a sokoban unicorn to max luck.
Eventually I reached the Medusa level, so I got back for the quest. To
kill the Cromatic Dragon I engraved E-word with a wand and wielded
Dragonbane I had received as a gift.
At this point I had found some speed boots, levitating boots and a
reflection shield (perseus), but I still hadn't found any sort of
sack/bag, even after thoroughly searching the mines, but I decided to
postpone a bit more breaking whisless, which almost cost me the game:
while tranfering my stash (strained) to the downstairs of Medusa I got
surrounded by gremlins, while over water. I put on a =oC and broke a
/oTeleport, but it was still a close call.

At the Valley I found a bag of holding, and finally decided to go for
wishless (although a second magic marker at Rodney's tower helped). At
the end of the Valley I also identified: "oLS, =FA, =Reg and =SD.

Before the ascension run I did the common preparations, such as
alchemy (163HP -> 400 HP) and also spent all my /oCM on a sacfest to
generate Vorpal blade. I was mostly using the Scepter, but wanted to
avoid Vorpal blade on the Astral plane.
As for the ascension run, it went smoothly, and even the water plane
was relatively short: only 500 turns and 1 Rodney appearance.

